  "source_text": "Title: The easiest way to make croissant! Why I didn't know this method before!\n\nChannel: Liza’s Delicious recipes\n\nVideo description:\n\nHello friends! Please turn on subtitles in the following in your language. Thanks for watching.\n\nThe easiest way to make croissant! Why I didn't know this method before!\n#croissantrecipe #croissant #baking \n\nIngredients:\n1/3 cup of warm water (80-90 ml).\n1 tbsp sugar (10g).\n1 tbsp dry yeast or instant yeast (8g).\n1/5 cup of warm milk (50 ml).\n2/3 tsp salt (4g).\n2 cups flour (250g).\nButter: 5 tbsp soft butter (50g) for dough and 15 tbsp soft butter for grease (150g).\n\nBake at 190° (375°F) for 20-25 minutes.\n\nThe result is light, airy, golden, flaky and buttery croissants! Bon appetit!\n\nTranscript (creator subtitles, en):\n\nQuick and easy butter croissants. 1/3 cup of warm water (80-90 ml). 1 tbsp sugar (10g). 1 tbsp dry yeast or instant yeast (8g). Mix the ingredients. Hello friends! If you like my videos follow me for more videos! Leave for 5 to 10 minutes. 1/5 cup of warm milk (50 ml). 2/3 tsp salt (4g). Mix the ingredients. 2 cups flour (250g). Mixing dough by hands. 5 tbsp soft butter (50g). Kneading for 6 minutes by hand. It calms me. I really enjoy kneading dough. Do you like kneading dough? Kneading helps smooth the dough out. Let the dough rest at room temperature for 1 hour. If it appears to be twice the original size, it's ready. Transfer the dough to a well-floured surface. Divide the dough into 8 equal portions. Take one piece and form a ball. Roll out the dough into a circle. Transfer the one circle to a well-floured dish. Grease with soft butter. Put on top a circle of dough. Grease with soft butter. Put on top a circle of dough again. Chill in fridge for one hour. Transfer the dough to a well-floured surface. Roll out the dough into a large rectangle. Friends, which country are you from? Roll out the dough well! You'll be rewarded with the best treat ever! Trim the edges. Slice the large rectangle into 6 triangles. Cut a small slit at the wide end of the triangle, then tightly roll up. Each croissant is different! This is wonderful! You agree with me? Transfer to a baking sheet. Let the dough rest at room temperature for 1 hour. Grease with egg. Bake at 190° (375°F) for 20-25 minutes. The result is light, airy, golden, flaky and buttery croissants! Bon appetit!",
  "raw_title": "The easiest way to make croissant! Why I didn't know this method before!",
